/*!
  \page example_cxx_binding_page Binding existing data structures

  This example shows how to use %Ponca on data stored in an existing data structure, without memory duplication. The
  input is a raw interlaced buffer storing, for each point, its position followed by its normal. The point type
  Ponca::PointPositionNormalBinding implements the \ref concepts_point "point concept" by mapping this buffer: a point
  is created on the fly for every neighbor, and only stores two `Eigen::Map` objects. The processing is otherwise the
  same as in \ref example_cxx_basic_page.

  Build and run:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_binding
  ./build/examples/cpp/ponca_binding
  \endcode

  See also \ref ponca_points_binding.

  \include cpp/ponca_binding.cpp
*/
